      "body": "#36006 got auto-closed by a linked PR.\r\n\r\nMore info on the infra side of things:\r\n\r\nI have configured two physically separate bitcoin core substitute servers for better availability (using [this module](https://github.com/willcl-ark/nix/tree/master/modules/bitcoin-core-guix-substitutes). One server evaluates the guix closure and builds it. Then uses `guix copy` to copy store items to the second server via ssh.\r\n\r\nWe could include the default substitute servers (https://bordeaux.guix.gnu.org https://ci.guix.gnu.org), but this makes the CI runs noticeably slower as these (slow) servers are queried even when not used/selected. These servers obviously will never include our custom compilers, which are the slowest thing to build, too.\r\n\r\nI tested a run with a single substitute server, shutting the server off _part way through_, and Guix didn't like that it _thought_ a substitute should be available but then wasn't and so failed. I think our use of `--fallback` protects us in the case that no substitute servers are available before the run begins; everything is just rebuilt, but have not tested this yet.\r\n\r\n",
